WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.245
Third-party resources are one of the
hardest parts of CSP design.

2
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:09.811
Applications often depend on CDNs,
analytics, tag managers,

3
00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:15.585
payment widgets, embedded media, maps,
chat tools, fonts, and external APIs.

4
00:00:15.665 --> 00:00:22.049
Each dependency may require scripts,
frames, images, styles, or network connections.

5
00:00:22.129 --> 00:00:26.357
CSP forces teams to name those
relationships explicitly,

6
00:00:26.437 --> 00:00:29.283
which can be uncomfortable but useful.

7
00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:33.591
If the application cannot explain why a
source is allowed,

8
00:00:33.671 --> 00:00:36.000
that source should be reviewed.

9
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.135
Overly broad allowlists reduce the value
of the policy.

10
00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:45.046
Allowing every subdomain of a large
provider, every HTTPS source,

11
00:00:45.126 --> 00:00:49.008
or broad wildcard patterns may make
deployment easy,

12
00:00:49.088 --> 00:00:53.575
but it also permits more behavior than the
application needs.

13
00:00:53.655 --> 00:00:59.952
Third-party scripts also carry supply
chain considerations because code loaded from

14
00:01:00.032 --> 00:01:02.879
an external origin can affect the page.

15
00:01:02.959 --> 00:01:08.049
CSP cannot make an untrusted script safe
once it is allowed to execute.

16
00:01:08.129 --> 00:01:13.910
It can, however, help limit which origins
are trusted and make unexpected loads

17
00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:14.680
visible.

18
00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:21.058
Maintaining an inventory of trusted
resource origins is a practical governance step.

19
00:01:21.138 --> 00:01:25.279
The inventory should identify why each
origin is needed,

20
00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:30.966
which feature uses it, which directive
allows it, who owns the relationship,

21
00:01:31.046 --> 00:01:34.066
and what happens if the provider changes.

22
00:01:34.146 --> 00:01:37.338
Frontend architecture choices matter too.

23
00:01:37.418 --> 00:01:42.249
Reducing tag sprawl, avoiding unnecessary
third-party scripts,

24
00:01:42.329 --> 00:01:45.521
bundling static assets where appropriate,

25
00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:50.260
and separating data from code all make CSP
simpler and stronger.
